{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/833865-one-off-idea-playing-werewolf-in-werewolf","id":833865,"title":"One-off idea - playing Werewolf in Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-20T08:59:33-08:00","id":833865,"title":"One-off idea - playing Werewolf in Werewolf","content":"So I had a random thought that it might be fun for a one-off game some time to play a game of Werewolf (the Mafia variant) in Werewolf: the Forsaken. I'm thinking players would either draw cards from a deck to randomly determine their roles as usual and then create characters based on their roles, or else use pregenerated characters for each role and assign them randomly. Then the story would follow the same basic structure as the party game. Each night is a scene or maybe a chapter, and the players interact in character to try to determine the werewolf's identity and execute them before they kill everyone off. But instead of just having a role and a simple rule to go with your role, you have a full CofD character and can use that character's stats and abilities as you see fit. It's a bit of a half-formed idea at this point, but I thought I'd bring it to the forums to see if anyone thinks it has promise or has any thoughts on how to flesh it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-20-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T11:42:51-08:00","id":833939,"title":"","content":"Ooh, fascinating. The biggest hurdle to manage, by my reckoning, is incorporation of the asymmetric features of the Mafia variant. Two ideas to throw in the pot to that effect:<br /> <br /> 1) All players write &quot;nighttime phase actions&quot; on a card or text the ST. The ST can then roll the relevant dice pools of the called actions while the human player reacts to the best of their abilities. This option isn't truly elegant, as it takes the most werewolfy parts of being a werewolf out of the hands of the players, but it's at least a talking point. Obviously, these orders don't need to just be written at night, merely at a certain defined interval that allows the werewolf characters to hide their doings without breaking character.<br /> <br /> 2) Play is digital only.This can allow a slew of information control so that the werewolf characters can act on their own accord at relevant intervals. If they're being covert, they can message the ST to handle an action like above, but you can also utilize ordered camera blackouts so that when a human is cornered alone with a werewolf, the two players get to rp it out.<br /> <br /> And an idea that has nothing to do with asymmetry:<br /> <br /> 3) Make a more thematic (rather than literal humans vs werewolves) interpretation of the Mafia variant: you're all playing a pack that has been infiltrated by Bale Hounds. Some of you play humans. Some of you are Uratha. And the Bale Hounds will do their best to hide among you. A more supernaturally-charged version of the Mafia game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","user":"Tilting Clock","date":".  Clarity of meaning 02-20-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","name":"Tilting Clock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T12:04:16-08:00","id":833966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tilting Clock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/833865-one-off-idea-playing-werewolf-in-werewolf?p=833939#post833939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, fascinating. The biggest hurdle to manage, by my reckoning, is incorporation of the asymmetric features of the Mafia variant. Two ideas to throw in the pot to that effect:<br /> <br /> 1) All players write &amp;quot;nighttime phase actions&amp;quot; on a card or text the ST. The ST can then roll the relevant dice pools of the called actions while the human player reacts to the best of their abilities. This option isn't truly elegant, as it takes the most werewolfy parts of being a werewolf out of the hands of the players, but it's at least a talking point. Obviously, these orders don't need to just be written at night, merely at a certain defined interval that allows the werewolf characters to hide their doings without breaking character.<br /> <br /> 2) Play is digital only.This can allow a slew of information control so that the werewolf characters can act on their own accord at relevant intervals. If they're being covert, they can message the ST to handle an action like above, but you can also utilize ordered camera blackouts so that when a human is cornered alone with a werewolf, the two players get to rp it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is along the same lines as my thinking as well. In-person I would probably do it more in the style of One Night Ultimate Werewolf. Play out the first phase as normal with all the card swapping mechanics and such, and then make characters based on the card you end up with, then play out the rest as a normal one-off CofD game without the day and night action mechanics. Online you could more easily manage the asymmetrical play. I'm actually thinking if we can work out a good way to handle this, and if there's interest I might be willing to run such a game in the PbP forums here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tilting Clock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/833865-one-off-idea-playing-werewolf-in-werewolf?p=833939#post833939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And an idea that has nothing to do with asymmetry:<br /> <br /> 3) Make a more thematic (rather than literal humans vs werewolves) interpretation of the Mafia variant: you're all playing a pack that has been infiltrated by Bale Hounds. Some of you play humans. Some of you are Uratha. And the Bale Hounds will do their best to hide among you. A more supernaturally-charged version of the Mafia game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, that would be a really cool variant too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T15:17:11-08:00","id":834081,"title":"","content":"I modeled a game of Clue into a game one time, and it was a blast. The slow dawning on my players' faces as they figured out how the routine was shaping up was worth the effort.<br /> <br /> Let us know how it turns out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}